{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"RCA confirmed (2026-09-03): `tests/e2e/test_editor_e2e.py::test_emitted_bpmn_has_no_illegal_ids` worker crashes are a pre-existing test/toolchain flake, not caused by `8eff-87c1-d09a-4893` / Gerrit 2592.\n\nEvidence:\n- CI crash fingerprint recurred twice on Gerrit 2592: run 33815705743 py3.13 logged `[gw0] node down: Not properly terminated`, then `worker 'gw0' crashed while running 'tests/e2e/test_editor_e2e.py::test_emitted_bpmn_has_no_illegal_ids'`, with coverage reporting a failed worker and no test assertion; run 33819616393 py3.11 logged the same node-down/crashed-worker signature.\n- Current `origin/main` reproduction worktree: `85ef5ad33ada9540d18bd17775bf2a521ef6ccbb` (= `origin/main`). The e2e fixture does lazy Node provisioning in test setup: `tests/e2e/conftest.py:47-58` runs `npm install` / `npm run build` inside session-scoped `bpmn_harness` when `node_modules` or `dist/roundtrip.mjs` is absent. Pytest's global timeout covers fixture setup (`pyproject.toml:719-720`, `timeout=300`, `timeout_method=thread`), and CI runs the default tier under xdist worksteal (`.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml:781-786`). The workflow comments document the failure mode: the thread timeout exits the worker, producing `node down: Not properly terminated` instead of a normal timeout failure (`.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml:772-777`).\n- Discriminating local experiments: cold toolchain + isolation with the normal 300s budget timed out in fixture setup after 300s while blocked in `subprocess.run([npm, \"install\"], cwd=_JS_DIR, ...)` (`tests/e2e/conftest.py:51-53`). Cold toolchain + xdist + deliberately-short `--timeout=10 --timeout-method=thread` reproduced the exact xdist crash signature: `[gw3] node down: Not properly terminated` and `worker 'gw3' crashed while running ...test_emitted_bpmn_has_no_illegal_ids` in 11.38s. With the toolchain preinstalled and bundle prebuilt, the same xdist command with `--timeout=10` passed in 1.50s. This rules out BPMN illegal-id assertion failure, BPMN serialization nondeterminism, and 8eff docs/scripts changes; the crash is caused by provisioning work happening inside the per-test timeout window.\n- 8eff/Gerrit 2592 patchset 2 only changes docs/ADR/API-stability/architecture and script-policy tests: `docs/adr/.numbers/0111`, `docs/adr/0111-no-internal-only-compatibility-shims.md`, `docs/adr/README.md`, `docs/api-stability.md`, `docs/architecture.md`, `tests/scripts/test_internal_shim_policy_docs.py`, `tests/scripts/test_no_internal_shim_policy.py`. It does not touch `tests/e2e/`, BPMN/editor code, Node harness code, pytest timeout config, or CI xdist command lines.\n\nClassification: (a) genuine pre-existing flaky/test-isolation/resource-timeout bug independent of 8eff. Not a provably transient infra-only fault: the class is reproducible locally by constraining the same pytest-timeout mechanism, and CI hit it on two interpreter shards. Defect origin: ticket `bold-abeyant-indri` (`73b8-2d79-3046-44ce`), commit `6a5c88027c59d3e24d3e4269838fb3c591a64240` (`Adopt standard test-hygiene tooling`) introduced the global fixture-covering pytest-timeout mechanism; the pre-existing lazy e2e provisioning then became capable of killing xdist workers when registry/install latency exceeded the budget.\n\nMinimal fix required: move e2e Node provisioning out of the `bpmn_harness` fixture/test timeout budget (prefer CI/local `make e2e-deps` using lockfile-based `npm ci` before pytest, plus a collection/session-level fallback that is not charged to an individual test item), and keep any fallback subprocesses explicitly bounded/diagnostic. Do not unblock 8eff with a blind `recheck`; either land this class fix first, or accept a targeted recheck only as a tactical retry with known residual flake risk, not because the evidence proves transient infra."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788484963851856733,"uuid":"5d0320d7-bcb9-4520-883a-6e5c2b26988d"}